Subject: [PATCH] # Enable Hybrid Multi-Group KV Transfer (Engine-Driven Path)
 for Qwen3.5/Gemma-Style models on Intel GPU
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Status: **draft / uncommitted** -- describes work-in-progress changes on top of
[`engine_driven_transfer_design.md`](engine_driven_transfer_design.md).

## 1. Motivation & What Changed

The engine-driven (XPU) transfer path originally assumed a single, uniform
KV cache group for the whole model: one shared block size, one shared
hidden dimension, one shared KV format. Hybrid models such as Qwen3.5 and
Gemma, which mix multiple KV cache groups, could not run on XPU under this
assumption.

This change adds engine-driven multi-group support for Qwen3.5/Gemma-style
hybrid models on XPU only (the CUDA IPC / lmcache-driven path is untouched):

- The worker can register **N independently-shaped LMCache groups** (own
  layer count, block size, hidden dim, KV format per group) instead of
  requiring every group to share one layout.
- Store/retrieve gather, transfer, and scatter each group using its own
  layout, concatenating wire data **group-major** .
- Null-chunk skipping: chunks vLLM has already nulled out (recurrent
  state before it's live, or sliding-window/GDN chunks outside the current
  window) are no longer stored or read back as garbage -- a new per-group,
  per-chunk mask excludes them from the transfer.

Non-hybrid (single-group) registrations keep working unchanged -- every new
code path collapses to the old single-group behavior when no groups are
registered.

## 2. Testing Result

**Platform:** Test on Intel PTL iGPU and B60.

**VLLM:** 0.26.0

**Test commands:**

vLLM server:

```bash
# block-size  Qwen3-8B: 1024 Qwen3.5-9B: 1024 gemma4-E4B-it: 1024
VLLM_SERVER_DEV_MODE=1 python3 -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \
  --model "$MODEL_PATH/$MODEL" \
  --dtype=float16 \
  --enforce-eager \
  --port 8000 \
  --block-size 1024 \
  --gpu-memory-util 0.7 \
  --kv-cache-memory-bytes 2G \
  --trust-remote-code \
  --enable-prefix-caching \
  --mamba-cache-mode align \
  --max_num_batched_tokens=1024 \
  --max_model_len 12000 \
  -tp=1 \
  --quantization fp8 \
  --served-model-name "$SERVE" \
  --kv-transfer-config '{"kv_connector":"LMCacheMPConnector","kv_role":"kv_both","kv_connector_extra_config":{"lmcache.mp.host":"tcp://localhost","lmcache.mp.port":6555,"lmcache.mp.mq_timeout":600,"lmcache.mp.heartbeat_interval":15}}' \
  --enable-prompt-tokens-details
```

LMCache server:

```bash
# --chunk-size Qwen3-8B: 1024 Qwen3.5-9B: 1024 gemma4-E4B-it: 2048
lmcache server \
  --port 6555 \
  --http-port 8090 \
  --l1-size-gb 30 \
  --eviction-policy LRU \
  --eviction-trigger-watermark 0.80 \
  --eviction-ratio 0.99 \
  --supported-transfer-mode auto \
  --shm-name lmcache_l1_pool_server \
  --chunk-size=1024
```

lmcache bench (vLLM L0 miss -> LMCache L1 hit, workload `prefix-suffix-tuner`):

```bash
# --psf-context-lengt Qwen3-8B: 7000 Qwen3.5-9B: 8000 gemma4-E4B-it: 28444
lmcache bench engine \
  --engine-url http://localhost:8000 \
  --workload prefix-suffix-tuner \
  --tokens-per-gb-kvcache 7000 \
  --psf-context-length 8000 \
  --psf-prefix-ratio 0.8 \
  --psf-thrash 8 \
  --no-interactive \
  --output-dir /tmp/psf_bench/baseline2 \
  --json
```


