## 3. Architecture Changes

### 3.1 Worker Side: One Layout -> Per-Group Plans


![Worker-side transfer flow: Before (one shared layout) vs. After (one plan per LMCache group)](hybrid_multi_group_worker_flow.png)

Before:

```text
EngineDrivenTransferContext
  register()
    -> one EngineDrivenContextMetadata (shared layout_desc, block_size)

  submit_store()
    -> prepare_store -> gather_paged_kv_to_cpu(all layers, one block size)
       -> commit_store

  submit_retrieve()
    -> prepare_retrieve -> scatter_cpu_to_paged_kv(all layers, one block size)
       -> commit_retrieve

AsyncEngineDrivenTransferContext.submit_store()  (pre-existing, #3808)
    -> prepare_store -> gather_paged_kv_to_cpu(all layers, one block size)
       runs in the background commit_executor
    -> staging buffers keyed by ONE (shape, dtype), since every chunk in a
       single-group store shares one shape
    -> commit_store
```

After:

```text
EngineDrivenTransferContext
  register()
    -> _build_group_transfer_plans(engine_group_infos)
       -> self._group_plans: list[GroupTransferPlan]
          (per group: layer_indices, blocks_per_chunk, chunk_shape,
           engine_kv_format -- cached once, not recomputed per transfer)
       -> single-group fallback: one plan with group_info=None when
          engine_group_infos is empty

  iter_transfer_groups()                   <-- shared fan-out point
    -> yields (plan, group_kv_caches, group_block_ids) per group
       (or the single-group fallback plan when no groups were registered)

  submit_store()
    -> iter_transfer_groups()
    -> _has_maskable_group() -> null_chunk_mask_from_groups()
       (attach null_chunk_mask to the key when any group is recurrent or
       sliding-window)
    -> prepare_store (server reserves slots / returns chunk_indices)
    -> for plan, group_kv_caches, group_block_ids in transfer_groups:
         slice flat out_buffers/chunk_indices onto this group via
         _select_group_chunks(); skip if this group has nothing selected
         gather_paged_kv_to_cpu() using THAT group's plan
           (blocks_per_chunk, chunk_shape, cached engine_kv_format)
    -> concatenate gathered chunks group-major
    -> commit_store

  submit_retrieve()
    -> iter_transfer_groups()
    -> _has_maskable_group() -> null_chunk_mask_from_groups()
    -> prepare_retrieve (server returns flat, group-major src_buffers,
       already shortened by any null-masked chunks)
    -> for plan, group_kv_caches, group_block_ids in transfer_groups:
         drop this group's null-masked block IDs via
         _select_live_scatter_chunks() to line up with the server's
         already-shortened chunk list
         scatter_cpu_to_paged_kv() using THAT group's plan
    -> commit_retrieve

AsyncEngineDrivenTransferContext.submit_store()  (pre-existing class, retrofitted)
    -> same iter_transfer_groups() fan-out, but the per-group gather loop
       runs in the background commit_executor; staging buffers are
       bucketed by (shape, dtype) since groups can have different shapes
```



### 3.2 Server Side: One Context -> Per-Group Contexts
![Server-side transfer flow: Before (one shared context) vs. After (one context per LMCache group), including the pickle/SHM split in commit_store](hybrid_multi_group_server_flow.png)

Before:

```text
EngineDrivenTransferModule
  register_kv_cache_engine_driven_context()
    -> one EngineDrivenContextEntry.metadata (shared layout_desc)

  prepare_store() / commit_store() / prepare_retrieve() / commit_retrieve()
    -> operate on entry.metadata directly (single layout, single set of
       object keys, single TransferStrategy call)
```

After:

```text
EngineDrivenTransferModule
  register_kv_cache_engine_driven_context()
    -> if engine_group_infos present:
         entry.metadata_by_group: list[EngineDrivenContextMetadata]
         (one per group, own layout_desc + block_size)
         + AttnWindowDesc registered via _make_attn_window_desc()
           (per-group sliding-window size, "attention"/"recurrent"/
           "standalone" kind)
       else:
         entry.metadata_by_group stays empty -> single-group fallback

  prepare_store() / prepare_retrieve()
    -> contexts = entry.metadata_by_group or [entry.metadata]  <-- decision point
    -> for group_id, context in enumerate(contexts):            <-- fan-out point
         resolve this group's object keys (_resolve_per_group_obj_keys)
         apply null_chunk_mask exclusion (_apply_null_chunk_mask)
         delegate to TransferStrategy for this group
         accumulate with a running chunk_offset
    -> concatenate slots/chunk_indices (store) or slots/chunks (retrieve)
       group-major

  commit_store()                          <-- pickle/SHM split on cpu_data
    -> if cpu_data == b"" (SHM mode):
         flatten all groups' object keys (_flatten_obj_keys)
         one strategy.commit_store_chunks() call, chunks=[]
           (worker already wrote into reserved slots; this only
           releases the shared write locks for every group at once)
       else (pickle mode):
         pickle.loads(cpu_data) once -> flat, group-major chunk list
         for group_id, context in enumerate(contexts):           <-- fan-out point
           slice this group's chunks out of the flat list via chunk_offset
           strategy.commit_store_chunks() for this group's slice
         result = AND of all groups' outcomes

  commit_retrieve()
    -> single strategy.commit_retrieve() call
       (SHM read locks for every group were accumulated under the same
       transfer key during prepare_retrieve, so one call releases them all;
       pickle mode has nothing to release)
```


`TransferStrategy` (`server_transfer.py`) gained `commit_store_chunks()` /
`prepare_retrieve_chunks()` so a multi-group caller can pass already-decoded
tensors instead of re-pickling per group, and `ShmTransferStrategy` now
accumulates reservations from multiple `prepare_store`/`prepare_retrieve`
calls (one per group) under the same transfer key, so a single
`commit_store`/`commit_retrieve` releases every group's locks together.

