- `gen_worker_flow.py` (272 lines) -- generates the §3.1 worker-side figure.
- `gen_server_flow.py` (253 lines) -- generates the §3.2 server-side figure.
- `hybrid_multi_group_worker_flow.{svg,png}` /
  `hybrid_multi_group_server_flow.{svg,png}` -- generated output embedded in
  §3.1 and §3.2. Regenerate with `python3 gen_worker_flow.py` and
  `python3 gen_server_flow.py` (requires `cairosvg`).

### `lmcache/v1/multiprocess/custom_types.py`

Pure data-model additions, no control-flow changes:
- `IPCCacheServerKey.null_chunk_mask: tuple[tuple[bool, ...], ...] | None` --
  per-group, per-chunk null mask for a store/retrieve call.
- `RegisterEngineDrivenContextPayload.engine_group_infos: list[EngineGroupInfo]`
  -- one entry per LMCache group (layer indices, `tokens_per_block`,
  sliding-window size, recurrent-state flag). Empty = single non-hybrid group.
- `RegisterEngineDrivenContextPayload.group_hidden_dim_sizes: list[int] | None`
  -- per-group override of the shared `hidden_dim_size`, since hybrid groups
  can pack K/V differently.

### `lmcache/v1/multiprocess/transfer_context/worker_transfer.py` (largest change)

- `register()` now builds `self._group_plans` via `_build_group_transfer_plans()`,
  precomputing each group's layer subset, block-size-adjusted
  `blocks_per_chunk`, `chunk_shape`, and pre-detected KV format once at
  registration time (avoids recomputation on every transfer).
- New `GroupTransferPlan` (frozen dataclass): one group's registration-time
  constants for gather/scatter.
- New `iter_transfer_groups()`: the fan-out point -- yields
  `(plan, group_kv_caches, group_block_ids)` per group, or a single
  single-group-fallback entry when no groups are registered.
- `submit_store()` / `submit_retrieve()` now loop over `iter_transfer_groups()`
  instead of assuming one group; slice flat `out_buffers`/`chunk_indices` per
  group via new `_select_group_chunks()` / `GroupChunkSelection`; compute and
  attach `null_chunk_mask` via `_has_maskable_group()` +
  `null_chunk_mask_from_groups()` when any group is recurrent or
  sliding-window.

### `lmcache/v1/multiprocess/transfer_context/async_engine_driven.py`

- `submit_store()`'s forward-thread setup now builds `transfer_groups` and
  computes the null-chunk mask before handing off to the background
  `commit_executor`.
- The background gather phase loops per group, slicing `out_buffers` /
  pinned staging buffers per group and using each group's own
  `engine_kv_format` / `chunk_shape`.
- `_release_staging()` now buckets returned tensors by `(shape, dtype)`
  instead of assuming every chunk shares one shape, since hybrid groups
  stage differently-shaped buffers.

### `lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/engine_driven_transfer.py`

- `register_kv_cache_engine_driven_context()` builds
  `EngineDrivenContextEntry.metadata_by_group` (one `EngineDrivenContextMetadata`
  per group) and, when groups are present, registers per-group layout
  descriptors plus an `AttnWindowDesc` (new `_make_attn_window_desc()`)
  instead of one shared `layout_desc`.
- `prepare_store()` / `commit_store()` / `prepare_retrieve()` / `commit_retrieve()`
  all loop over `contexts = entry.metadata_by_group or [entry.metadata]`,
  resolving per-group object keys, applying `null_chunk_mask` exclusion
  before reservation, and concatenating results group-major with a running
  `chunk_offset`.
- `commit_store()` gained a fast SHM path (`commit_store_chunks` with empty
  `chunks`, releasing locks only) alongside the pickle path, which now
  decodes the wire payload once and slices it per group.
- Session timing keys (`store_start_time` / `retrieve_start_time`) are now
  keyed by `(name, key.start, key.end)` instead of a fixed string, since
  multi-group chunks of the same request can have interleaved
  prepare/commit calls.

### `lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/server_transfer.py`

- New abstract `TransferStrategy.commit_store_chunks()` /
  `prepare_retrieve_chunks()` -- let multi-group callers pass already-decoded
  tensors instead of round-tripping pickle per group.
- `PickleTransferStrategy.commit_store()` / `prepare_retrieve()` now
  delegate to the chunk-based variants.
- `ShmTransferStrategy.prepare_store()` / `prepare_retrieve()` now
  accumulate reservations from multiple per-group calls under the same
  transfer key instead of overwriting, so one `commit_store`/`commit_retrieve`
  releases every group's locks; `_release_write_locks()` factored out.

### Tests

- `tests/v1/multiprocess/test_engine_driven_multi_group.py` (worker-side,
  1150 lines): per-group helper unit tests, `iter_transfer_groups` fallback
  / fan-out / error cases, end-to-end `submit_store`/`submit_retrieve`
  round-trips across two groups (group-major concatenation, correct scatter
  targeting, SHM buffer narrowing, skipping fully-cached groups),
  null-chunk-mask attachment for recurrent/sliding-window groups on both
  sync and async paths, and a regression test for a length-mismatch bug in
  masked retrieves.
- `tests/v1/multiprocess/test_engine_driven_transfer_multi_group_server.py`
  (server-side, 753 lines): per-group registration/layout correctness,
  `AttnWindowDesc` derivation, group-major flatten/split/merge correctness
  for store and retrieve, miss-in-any-group failing the whole retrieve,
  single-`commit_retrieve` finalizing all groups.
- `tests/v1/multiprocess/test_engine_driven_transfer.py` (existing file, +90
  lines): server-side `null_chunk_mask` consumption --
  `test_server_prepare_store_excludes_null_masked_chunk` and
  `test_server_commit_store_slices_chunks_for_null_masked_group`.
